  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I'm an avatar creator that infrequently uses my Quest 2 to test my creations. \n\nWhether it's game updates, or the long periods of time between logging into my Quest, it loves to have me sign in every time I launch VRC in my Quest 2.\n\nI like to use long randomized passwords with special characters for every account. Manually typing out a 20+ character password by hand in VR every time is extremely tedious.\n\nChanging it to something simple is not an option, especially when you consider that one of my avatars is on the global public avatar selection! Last thing I want is that account be compromised.\n\nIt would be nice if you can roll the login and two factor into one login step IF the user has previously logged in on that device previously, and the session has since been invalidated/expired.\n\nThis way it's still secure - I still have to enter my very long password on new devices, and quickly re-authenticate on existing devices.",
